ts and also you make sure  that you're safe because nothing really  explodes in this environment however  there's some drawbacks in the sense that  when you're working with the gloves here  and it takes about two to three times  longer to do any process we try to use  an entirely new category of electrolytes  we were really lucky to get some really  great data and now we're trying to push  it even further to see if we can  increase the capacity and the multitude  of ways we develop something that is  close to $100 per kilowatt hour now so  it's bringing in the alternative energy  sources and also it's going to allow the  grid to be a lot more energy efficient  so it's cutting on both regimes and when  you see that come together that's like a  pretty amazing feat  with this new device it's gonna spark a  new economy because private homes could  even store energy at night and then sell  it back to the grid the next morning I  think a lot of the consistency that's  been in my undergraduate experience has  been in research and getting the skills  to learn how to solve new and  challenging problems
 

